                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9706a34f-f0d8-313d-91b7-c3f6fb199ddf",
                        "entry_id": "29c847a1-f0d1-3180-bbd7-fe1b4422b578",
                        "glosses": [
                            "imię męskie"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "80468ea4-f6c7-4242-a9a7-e61ff5aa3ec6",
                                "sense_id": "9706a34f-f0d8-313d-91b7-c3f6fb199ddf",
                                "text": "Ci, którzy byli na zamku, wydali Jonatanowi zakładników, a on zwrócił ich rodzicom"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24dbd824-b004-4861-b729-760e8edbe229",
                        "source_entry_id": "29c847a1-f0d1-3180-bbd7-fe1b4422b578",
                        "source_sense_id": "9706a34f-f0d8-313d-91b7-c3f6fb199ddf",
                        "target_lang_word": "Jonathan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Jonathan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9514426-da44-3d15-b58d-e4c33497b53b",
                                        "entry_id": "202c52b6-811f-3426-8676-f9f83ede11d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A son of Saul, first mentioned in 1 Samuel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44d29b52-3d18-456d-a49e-a8e12af7c25f",
                                                "sense_id": "f9514426-da44-3d15-b58d-e4c33497b53b",
                                                "text": "And it came to pass, when he had made an end to speaking unto Saul, that the soul of Jonathan was knit with the soul of David, and Jonathan loved him as his own soul."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eec58f23-f3aa-3d28-8df0-afc12ee1f9dd",
                                        "entry_id": "202c52b6-811f-3426-8676-f9f83ede11d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Jonathan Apphus, a son of Mattathias, brother of Joannan Caddis, Simon Thassi, Judas Maccabeus and Eleazar Avara."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d55d6959-b80c-44fe-8065-a82918c17d00",
                                                "sense_id": "eec58f23-f3aa-3d28-8df0-afc12ee1f9dd",
                                                "text": "Then Jonathan and Simon took Judas their brother, and buried him in the sepulchre of his fathers in Modin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b903e851-69df-3076-a694-ea3ccf39868a",
                                        "entry_id": "202c52b6-811f-3426-8676-f9f83ede11d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name from Hebrew of biblical origin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2c3a135-f832-44c0-acde-5db76e235e59",
                                                "sense_id": "b903e851-69df-3076-a694-ea3ccf39868a",
                                                "text": "“Well indeed,” said Foley, “’tis a mystery to me how the sergeant puts up with her. If any woman up and called me an outlandish name like Jonathan when everyone knew my name was plain John I’d do fourteen days for her - by God, I would, and a calendar month.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af40cd8b-be80-4359-8014-f923b61d923d",
                                                "sense_id": "b903e851-69df-3076-a694-ea3ccf39868a",
                                                "text": "So I’d change to names I really like. I mean, Jonathan. If I ever have a son I’m going to call him Jonathan, so I’d have that. And then I like monosyllabic surnames that aren’t too common, so I’d have Dean or Bell or King. There you are, how about Jonathan King?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2268b9ca-dabd-40e4-98e6-a5762005d101",
                                                "sense_id": "b903e851-69df-3076-a694-ea3ccf39868a",
                                                "text": "It is billed as a one-way trip, which by definition will make the Most Interesting Man, played till now by 77-year-old Jonathan Goldsmith, no longer the most interesting man in this world."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d932730e-37ac-3918-b8f6-2b3c35cf1f6e",
                                        "entry_id": "202c52b6-811f-3426-8676-f9f83ede11d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname from Hebrew."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Jonathan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1222960-b38f-32ba-9aa2-35beda98eaed",
                                        "entry_id": "d736cc12-10cf-33c9-9438-a241805b9d77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An apple cultivar from New York."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00948a9a-2aed-4100-8e78-9873f3cfba95",
                                                "sense_id": "a1222960-b38f-32ba-9aa2-35beda98eaed",
                                                "text": "For example, Jonathans are tart and great for baking."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef5bd799-918b-3fa8-b603-2639a00f6f9a",
                                        "entry_id": "d736cc12-10cf-33c9-9438-a241805b9d77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An American; a Yank; Brother Jonathan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64e30c53-4241-45de-bf97-bd880ef17e55",
                                                "sense_id": "ef5bd799-918b-3fa8-b603-2639a00f6f9a",
                                                "text": "Here crashed a sturdy oath of stout John Bull,\nWho damned away his eyes as heretofore;\nThere Paddy brogued “By Jasus!”—“What’s your Wull?”\nThe temperate Scot exclaimed; the French Ghost swore\nIn certain terms I shan’t translate in full,\nAs the first Coachman will; and midst the roar\nThe voice of Jonathan was heard to express,\n“Our president is going to war, I guess.”—"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18b7e53e-492c-4967-80ba-0a1a41f3e0cd",
                                                "sense_id": "ef5bd799-918b-3fa8-b603-2639a00f6f9a",
                                                "text": "The best single source of comment on Marble's capacities as a low comedian, as with the other Yankees, is the record of his London reception. […] One viewer thought it was not as outrageous as Jonathans usually are, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c08753d3-d342-312a-b8d2-b7ea61e67be7",
                                        "entry_id": "d736cc12-10cf-33c9-9438-a241805b9d77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "penis"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "18348561-dd3f-4451-affd-948a575fa1c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "29c847a1-f0d1-3180-bbd7-fe1b4422b578",
                        "source_sense_id": "9706a34f-f0d8-313d-91b7-c3f6fb199ddf",
